# Both Dockerfiles use the repository root as build context:
#   docker build -f gateway/Dockerfile .
#   docker build -f control-plane/Dockerfile .
# Keep the context small and deterministic; generated artifacts are rebuilt in
# the images and host-specific dependencies must not leak in.

.git
.github
.omh
.idea
.vscode
.env

# Python bytecode / test caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
control-plane/.venv
control-plane/tests

# Rust build output
gateway/target

# UI dependencies and build output (the image builds these from source)
ui/node_modules
ui/dist
ui/.vite
ui/test-results
ui/playwright-report
ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
ui/e2e
ui/playwright.config.ts

# Not needed by either image
bench/*
# ... except the crate the gateway's dev-dependencies name: cargo resolves its manifest
# (and, for `cargo test`, builds it) while loading the workspace, so `docker build -f
# gateway/Dockerfile` needs the sources but never its build output.
!bench/mock-upstream
bench/mock-upstream/target
deploy
docs
tests
scripts
